.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt POSTURE 8
.Os Werewolf
.Sh NAME
.Nm posture
.Nd report the running machine's protections
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl extended
.Op Fl Fl attack
.Op Fl Fl no-cache
.Op Fl Fl verbose
.Op Fl Fl json | Fl Fl line | Fl Fl summary
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility checks kernel protections, processes, filesystems and network policy.
It reports passes, failures and checks it cannot perform, with reasons.
On Werewolf it also checks the machine seal and service confinement.
Other Linux systems receive the applicable generic checks.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "--no-cache"
.It Fl Fl extended
Include protections Werewolf deliberately leaves optional, such as forced
CPU mitigations and wiping freed memory.
.It Fl Fl attack
Run additional intrusion probes.
These expect the kernel to refuse access; use only when testing is intended.
.It Fl Fl no-cache
Do not use the boot report for checks this invocation cannot perform.
Report those checks as skipped.
.It Fl Fl verbose
Write phases, timings and walk progress to standard error.
.It Fl Fl json
Write JSON, including the source, expected value, observation and comparison.
.It Fl Fl line
Write one line with failure identifiers, counts and JSON.
.It Fl Fl summary
Print the login summary: identity, state, counts and declared gaps.
.El
.Pp
Without a format option, output is human-readable text.
Results taken from the boot report are marked as cached.
Running as root permits more checks; some checks require the boot service's
context even when the caller is root.
.Pp
When invoked as
.Pa /etc/sv/posture/run ,
.Nm
waits for services to settle, writes the boot report and login message,
then takes itself down.
Checks may leave refusal records in the kernel log and console.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width WEREWOLF_CHECK
.It Ev WEREWOLF_CHECK
The value 1 enables intrusion probes, as does the kernel argument
.Li werewolf.check=1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /run/werewolf/posture.json
Boot report used for cached results.
.It Pa /run/werewolf/motd
Boot login message.
.It Pa /usr/share/werewolf/weaknesses
Failures the image declares and excuses.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is 1 if any check fails, including an excused failure,
and 0 if no check fails.
Invalid arguments produce status 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl posture --summary
.Dl posture --json
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fence 8 ,
.Xr leash 8 ,
.Xr seal 8
